# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project using the latest official documentation from Vercel.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added**: `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 to dependencies
- **Modified**: `package.json` - Added the @vercel/analytics package
- **Modified**: `pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated with new dependencies (1166 packages total)

### 2. Analytics Integration
- **Modified**: `src/app/layout.tsx`
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component before closing `</body>` tag
  - Follows Next.js App Router pattern as specified in Vercel documentation

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
- Identified this as a **Next.js 16.2.6** project using the **App Router** pattern
- Used **pnpm** as the package manager (v10.34.3)

### Configuration Approach
According to the latest Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):
1. For Next.js App Router projects, the Analytics component should be imported from `@vercel/analytics/next`
2. The component should be placed in the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`)
3. The component should be added before the closing `</body>` tag

### Code Placement
The `<Analytics />` component was added at the end of the body section, after the main content and skip link, ensuring it doesn't interfere with existing functionality while properly tracking page views.

## Verification Steps Completed

1. ✅ **TypeScript Compilation**: Passed with no errors (`npx tsc --noEmit --skipLibCheck`)
2. ✅ **ESLint**: Passed with only pre-existing warnings (none related to Analytics changes)
3. ⚠️ **Build**: The full build requires Sanity CMS environment variables which are not related to Analytics changes
4. ℹ️ **Tests**: No test suite configured in the project

## Next Steps for Deployment

To enable Web Analytics on Vercel:
1. Navigate to your project's Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
2. Click the "Enable" button to activate Web Analytics
3. Deploy this updated code to Vercel
4. Verify tracking is active by checking browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

## Notes

- The Analytics component will only send tracking data when deployed to Vercel (not in local development)
- No additional configuration is needed unless you want to customize tracking behavior
- The component is lightweight and won't impact performance
- All changes preserve existing code structure and styling
